  partName: Bolt (7)
  description: The Bolt (7) is a tiny, compact fastener located at the top-center-center
    of the engine, made of Material.002, which plays a crucial role in securing various
    components together, ensuring the engine's structural integrity, and its compact
    shape allows for efficient use of space. Its small size belies its importance,
    as it helps to maintain the engine's overall stability. Interestingly, the Bolt
    (7) is designed to withstand high torque forces.
